  "question": "Is our 30-day evaluation cycle stricter than Part 2.2 requires?",
  "answer": "No, your 30-day evaluation cycle is **stricter** than the standard requires.\n\nThe standard (CIP-007-6 R2 Part 2.2) sets the evaluation interval at **at least once every 35 calendar days** [csection-7700dd5499cead0994ec]. Your internal procedure (LSPG Security Patch Management Procedure, Section 3.3.1) mandates a review **at least once every thirty-five (35) calendar days** [isection-21a30e0d44708f5dfdce].\n\nWait, looking closely at your question and the documents:\n- **The Standard** requires an evaluation at least once every **35 days** [csection-7700dd5499cead0994ec].\n- **Your Procedure** (Section 3.3.1) also specifies **35 days** [isection-21a30e0d44708f5dfdce].\n\nHowever, you asked about a **30-day** cycle. If your actual operational practice is to perform this every 30 days, then you are indeed using less latitude than NERC grants by shortening the window from 35 days to 30 days. This is a permitted instance of intentional strictness.\n\nIf you meant to ask if the 35-day requirement in your procedure is stricter than the standard, it is not; they are currently aligned at the 35-day threshold.\n\nCited sections:\n- csection-7700dd5499cead0994ec (CIP-007-6 R2 Part 2.2 requirement text)\n- isection-21a30e0d44708f5dfdce (LSPG Security Patch Management Procedure, Section 3.3.1)",
